# Delighted Halfling: "Spend this mana only to cast a legendary spell, and that spell can't be countered." The
# protection belongs to the spell that was cast with that mana (CR 106.6a-b), not to every legendary spell: on turn 3 Bot1
# casts Cecil, Dark Knight with a Swamp, with the Halfling untapped and unused, and Bot2's Counterspell counters it. (The
# existing scenario shows the same Counterspell failing against Cecil cast with the Halfling's mana.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Delighted Halfling
Swamp
Cecil, Dark Knight
Forest x3
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Island x4
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Delighted Halfling.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Cecil, Dark Knight.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Cecil, Dark Knight)
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Cecil, Dark Knight
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Swamp; Delighted Halfling
